---
/**
 * Fee waterfall for the page's worked example — the site had ZERO <figure>/<img>/<svg> diagrams,
 * and multi-modal pages are measurably more likely to be selected by AI answer surfaces.
 *
 * Numbers are hard-tied to the "Worked example" section above it (0.5 BTC, $60k → $72k, 0.1% both
 * sides). If that example changes, change these with it — a diagram that disagrees with the prose
 * beside it is worse than no diagram.
 */
---
<figure class="diagram">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 720 300"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="waterfall-title waterfall-desc"
    preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
  >
    <title id="waterfall-title">What a 0.5 BTC trade from $60,000 to $72,000 actually returns</title>
    <desc id="waterfall-desc">
      Two bars drawn to the same scale. The gross gain of $6,000 and the net profit of $5,934 are almost
      the same height: the $66 paid in entry and exit fees is 1.1% of the gain. The return is 19.76%,
      measured against the $30,030 actually committed rather than the $30,000 nominally invested.
    </desc>

    <line x1="60" y1="238" x2="690" y2="238" class="axis" />

    <!-- Bars are proportional: 180px = $6,000, so $5,934 = 178px. -->
    <rect x="130" y="58" width="150" height="180" rx="4" class="bar bar-gain" />
    <text x="205" y="46" class="lbl lbl-value">+$6,000</text>
    <text x="205" y="262" class="lbl">What the price move implies</text>

    <rect x="440" y="60" width="150" height="178" rx="4" class="bar bar-net" />
    <text x="515" y="46" class="lbl lbl-value">$5,934</text>
    <text x="515" y="262" class="lbl">What actually lands</text>
    <text x="515" y="156" class="lbl lbl-inbar">19.76% ROI</text>

    <!-- the gap, annotated because at this scale it is almost invisible -->
    <path d="M296 58 H424" class="tie" />
    <path d="M296 60 H424" class="tie" />
    <path d="M360 58 V60" class="gap" />
    <text x="360" y="106" class="lbl lbl-fee lbl-value">−$66 in fees</text>
    <text x="360" y="126" class="lbl lbl-fee">$30 entry + $36 exit</text>
    <text x="360" y="146" class="lbl lbl-fee">= 1.1% of the gain</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    Fees are not what makes this trade different from the chart —{' '}<strong>$66</strong>{' '}is 1.1% of the gain.
    The number that moves is the denominator: the ROI is <strong>19.76%</strong> because <strong>$30,030</strong>{' '}
    was committed, not the $30,000 you meant to invest.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .diagram {
    margin: 24px 0;
  }

  .diagram svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    max-width: 720px;
    display: block;
  }

  .diagram figcaption {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: 10px;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .axis {
    stroke: var(--color-border);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .bar-gain { fill: var(--color-primary); opacity: 0.28; }
  .bar-net  { fill: var(--color-primary); }

  .gap {
    stroke: #b45309;
    stroke-width: 3;
  }

  .tie {
    stroke: var(--color-border);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-dasharray: 4 4;
    fill: none;
  }

  .lbl {
    fill: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    text-anchor: middle;
    font-family: inherit;
  }

  .lbl-value {
    fill: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .lbl-fee { fill: #b45309; }

  .lbl-inbar {
    fill: #fff;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  :global([data-theme='dark']) .bar-fee,
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .lbl-fee { fill: #fbbf24; }
</style>
